{
  "description": "Joining a Camfrog room by display name, the join snapshot of members (0x41 burst), and a failed join.",
  "grounding": "v1 room_control.py drives the Join Room dialog (accepts id or display name; window title is '<Display>, Topic: ...', not the room id). The c2s JOIN (0x00) names the room id; the server's 'You are now logged in' line marks the room as usable. 0x41 user-list entries carry login + display name; group headers split members (on cam) from lurkers. A missing room shows 'Room name is not found in the active chat room list.'",
  "frames": [
